       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and I don't know of any clinical situation where it would be appropriate. A patient who got it would be at high risk of severe liver injury or liver failure, and the damage can be irreversible before symptoms show.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. The maximum is 4 g/day, and many services use 3 g/day.\n- **Enter a different dose** if you tell me what you need.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy.** If you're treating something unusual, such as a protocol I don't know about, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology can review it. If the order is meant to be a different drug or a different unit, such as mg versus mcg, I can re-enter it correctly.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
